#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166592 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/id #uuid "181b2a5e-7caf-5527-8602-e67a945affde" :question/math-academy-id "e-8337" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = 2\\arsinh{x^2},$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsinh x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({x}^{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ce19d882-3c04-5ef1-8393-7de582df188d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8338" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =\\arcosh(x+1),$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcosh x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(x+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (x+1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+2x+1)-1}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x+2)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d5eeb5a1-4bfd-5f1e-b261-548c91eec64b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8339" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\artanh{4x},$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\artanh x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{(4x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(4x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-16{x}^{2}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1-16{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57d851ce-44b5-5713-ba65-7f5a9cc1122f" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "7cd3958b-aa1c-5c9a-b2ef-a21002aa7ff1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8340" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $w(x) = e^{2x}\\artanh{x},$ then $w'(x)=2e^{2x}\\artanh{x} + y(x).$ What is $y(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = e^{2x}$ and $v(x)=\\artanh{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{{\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{1-{x}^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{y(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y(x) = \\dfrac{e^{2x}}{1 - x^2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2b3cf5-7996-5a83-8016-0d37e8dd76db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{4x^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de2b3cf5-7996-5a83-8016-0d37e8dd76db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{4x^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517907} :answer-field/id #uuid "55157626-6033-5874-9ef3-053348b5fbb5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cb35406-f881-5edb-97ef-a6166561d9a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-337912" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=5\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(5\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a5b82a-32ba-5916-9e64-71bad821a989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{16x^{12}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44a5b82a-32ba-5916-9e64-71bad821a989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{16x^{12}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517622} :answer-field/id #uuid "6235e9dc-58a1-59ae-99c9-7e3dc3328c5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81194d8a-eb61-596d-a974-e9c1b95b27d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-342186" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $40{x}^{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}-1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57d851ce-44b5-5713-ba65-7f5a9cc1122f" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5132a52-9a35-59bb-b61d-b459caa0c29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{e^{2x}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5132a52-9a35-59bb-b61d-b459caa0c29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{e^{2x}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517889} :answer-field/id #uuid "2359561c-3d9c-533b-8276-68f929336a72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea0760db-381e-5949-ad3f-4c6362ce39c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342829" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=7\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}\\,+$ | $7{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={(7\\sqrt{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\text{arsinh}\\,({e}^{x})+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {({e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+\\frac{7{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57d851ce-44b5-5713-ba65-7f5a9cc1122f" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0c2e13-f46b-5cc2-a1f8-4fae6a1f6c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{(1-x^{4})\\ln x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0c2e13-f46b-5cc2-a1f8-4fae6a1f6c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{(1-x^{4})\\ln x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517749} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6519ced-6442-570a-bd64-3c6fcf3d8465" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75d28ef3-1631-5b9b-9daa-067de055774b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342834" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}  $-\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the quotient rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(\\frac{u}{v})}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{2})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{4}}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{(1-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf9422de-70d7-5b56-86c9-b6e0e3f8ac48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{16x^{12}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf9422de-70d7-5b56-86c9-b6e0e3f8ac48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{16x^{12}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517855} :answer-field/id #uuid "7980ba46-cdbd-57c7-a587-1058e543ca1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e33df1c-2868-500a-90eb-4948dc41205c" :question/math-academy-id "q-344305" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $8{x}^{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a329f99-1cb4-5ae5-986d-04046d4da53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517566} {:answer/id #uuid "2eaac038-f9e7-574a-9d3b-55268419a77d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517577} {:answer/id #uuid "34ca7eb5-470d-5de1-a985-de106f49a368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517592} {:answer/id #uuid "5151a771-88dc-542b-a9ae-7d62e4b4c00a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517647} {:answer/id #uuid "83532860-31ea-58e2-b9f9-6d535dda8bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34ca7eb5-470d-5de1-a985-de106f49a368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517592} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d14d448-a840-5321-9b6a-51cdd2f8b8d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d81cff16-2de4-5af9-90cd-bc5738649620" :question/math-academy-id "q-95242" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}+1}}\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dfa4edf-fd9d-5a8f-a626-7170364756b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{1-4{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517641} {:answer/id #uuid "89ad944e-2be0-56d8-9333-f1471c3d89eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{6{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517746} {:answer/id #uuid "92cf951f-ffe1-52cb-8388-109ef99e7472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517765} {:answer/id #uuid "97d1c47e-bdee-5dd8-9638-5da53d198c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{6{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517776} {:answer/id #uuid "aa289fc3-789c-5683-9e2f-a94eb4e15b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6{x}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92cf951f-ffe1-52cb-8388-109ef99e7472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517765} :answer-field/id #uuid "212e29fd-c89d-59da-8733-ca9e159bf6c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70dcb121-2c51-5a9a-a8d4-5a609e0f6393" :question/math-academy-id "q-95515" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-6{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eac5166-dabb-580e-b725-9123713934f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x(3-2x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517578} {:answer/id #uuid "34c509d9-c9e3-5e5a-96bf-5cdd105d47dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517591} {:answer/id #uuid "38d279e8-7cae-5b93-951c-3a28c5addc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2x(2-3x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517600} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd1ece5-ab7e-5496-92a9-91b0efce86bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x(2x-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517874} {:answer/id #uuid "d5415a38-3db7-5d44-8a65-954ad5158627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(3x-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34c509d9-c9e3-5e5a-96bf-5cdd105d47dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517591} :answer-field/id #uuid "234ebf93-a04c-5d8d-8e1c-b425df18a6da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96d64ea4-0cd9-5375-8219-9bae598e5ccf" :question/math-academy-id "q-96442" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(3x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(3x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6x-9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
